{\H0.91667x;NOTES:\P1) CONKLIN RECOMMENDS THAT ALL MAIN AISLE WAYS SHOULD BE 44" WIDE AND ALL INTERNAL AISLE WAYS SHOULD BE 36" WIDE.  ANY AISLES THAT ARE NOT WITHIN THESE MEASUREMENTS ARE THE CLIENT'S DECISION AND RESPONSIBILITY.  IT IS THE RESPONSI
  3
BILITY OF THE CLIENT TO VERIFY THAT ALL AISLE WAY DIMENSIONS MEET LOCAL BUILDING CODES.\P2) CONKLIN WILL NOT ACCEPT RESPONSIBILITY FOR ANY ERROR(S) IN INTERPRETATION OF THIS DRAWING, AND WE STRONGLY RECOMMEND A THOROUGH REVIEW.\P3) MODIFICATION OF FU
  3
RNITURE PARTS IS NOT APPROVED UNLESS OTHERWISE NOTED.  UNAUTHORIZED ALTERATIONS MAY VOID WARRANTY AND IMPACT FUNCTIONALITY.\P}4) BUILDING SHELL WAS IMPORTED AND SCALED TO FULL SIZE FROM CLIENT PROVIDED PDF.  CONKLIN WILL NOT BE RESPONSIBLE FOR FURNIT
  3
URE FIT ISSUES.  RECOMMEND VERIFYING ALL DIMENSIONS FOR PROPER FURNITURE FIT BEFORE ORDERING.\P5) COMPLETE ROOM DIMENSIONS, INCLUDING DOORS, WINDOWS, AND COLUMNS (SIZES AND LOCATIONS), WERE NOT PROVIDED.  CONKLIN WILL NOT BE RESPONSIBLE FOR FURNITURE
  1
 FIT ISSUES.  RECOMMEND VERIFYING ALL DIMENSIONS FOR PROPER FURNITURE FIT BEFORE ORDERING.\P6) CHANGES TO BUILDING PLAN ARE SHOWN FOR REFERENCE ONLY, NOT FOR CONSTRUCTION PURPOSES.
